  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top 4 performers all use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile, with config_029 (transformer+weighted) leading at 0.7250. All four aggregation×fusion combinations for this encoder pair have been tested, so no further gains are expected within that sub-space. The remaining untested scvi_n200+imagenet_vit_l configs (034, 036) are singleprofile variants that remove the aggregation step. Question: This experiment tests whether the multiprofile aggregation step is truly necessary or whether a single profile with the strong scvi_n200+imagenet_vit_l encoders and weighted fusion can approach the multiprofile results. Rationale: As the final experiment, the primary goal is to confirm the best result (0.7250) is robust and to minimize total GPU cost. config_036 uses the best-performing RNA and image encoders with weighted fusion (slightly favored in the evidence), and as a singleprofile model with no aggregation layer, it is expected to be the cheapest remaining option (~2-3 GPU hours vs. 3-5 for multiprofile+transformer configs). While it is unlikely to surpass 0.7250, it is the most cost-effective use of the last slot and provides a useful lower-bound on the contribution of multiprofile aggregation."
}

